WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.870
Step 1. Open the encounter Overview. You view allergies on its Allergies panel,

1.2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.143
and across encounters in the clinical history.

1.3
00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:13.556
On the patient's Encounters tab, select View Encounter.

2.1
00:00:13.556 --> 00:00:16.405
Step 2. Find the Allergies panel.

2.2
00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:22.811
The panel header shows how many allergies it lists, for example 3 recorded.

3.1
00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:29.044
Step 3. Read the allergies in the panel. The Status column is the clinical status,

3.2
00:00:29.044 --> 00:00:32.754
and Verification is the verification status.

4.1
00:00:32.754 --> 00:00:38.487
Step 4. Open the menu of an allergy. Select the info button on its row.

4.2
00:00:38.487 --> 00:00:44.547
See Note shows the note, and Reported by shows who recorded the allergy.

5.1
00:00:44.547 --> 00:00:50.116
Step 5. Open the clinical history. In the panel header, select History.

5.2
00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:54.213
The clinical history opens on its Allergies tab.

6.1
00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:56.881
Step 6. Read the Allergies tab.

6.2
00:00:56.881 --> 00:01:02.608
It groups the allergies by year, then by the date each was created.

7.1
00:01:02.608 --> 00:01:08.579
Step 7. Leave the clinical history. In an allergy's menu, select Go to Encounter.

7.2
00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:14.518
It opens the Overview of the encounter where the allergy form was last saved.
